; Move the actor in a direction
;
; Default handler (VerbHandlers) of the ten direction verbs (go north ... go down;
; CommandId holds DIR_NORTH to DIR_DOWN), also entered by run (#R$8FAD). The actor is
; the Subject: the player or an NPC acting from its script. It has three parts:
; $8D9D chooses the direction, #R$8DAB moves through the exit and #R$8E12 is the
; arrival.
; .
; Direction: in the dark (#R$95ED) the player cannot choose; CommandId becomes a random
; direction 1-10. A way out of a holder is refused unless the holder is a character
; (then the actor is set free of it); an actor inside a barrel or a boat cannot walk.
; TakeWeight is what the actor weighs plus what it carries (#R$9CE8). The exit comes
; from #R$9F08. Without an exit (or with destination 0) the command is refused
; (#R$9F76: "<subj> cannot go north."); but in the dark the player blunders into a wall:
; the player's strength (record +5) is halved, "But fall and hit your head.", and when
; the halving leaves 0, "But fall and smash your skull." and the game ends (#R$90D2).
; .
; Obstacle: #R$8E85 tests the exit's obstacle and the destination's capacity. Blocked:
; refused. Too small or too full: "<the thing> is too small (full) for <subj> to
; enter." (the too small message takes its word from record bytes +2,+3 of the obstacle,
; its weight, which is a bug: it prints a wrong word; see the findings).
; .
; Arrival (#R$8E12, also entered by #R$9BDD for a player carried to a new place, with TakeId
; and B set): when really performing, the actor's location slot (record +$10) becomes
; B, what it carries comes along (#R$9BDD) and an NPC is done (its movement is shown by
; #R$9ACD). For the player the arrival handler of the destination runs (ArrivalHandlers),
; and unless it is dark the destination is described: the first time (location flag
; LOC_VISITED not yet set) the flag is set, the score is raised by the value found for the
; location id in #R$8D6E (that table is keyed by location id, not by treasure) and the
; full description with picture follows (#R$9630); a visited location gets the short
; one (#R$96A8).
; .
; Hardware: none directly; the description may show a picture and wait for a key.
;
; B New location id ($8E12 only)
; IY Record of the actor ($8E12 only; #R$9BDD enters with the IY of its own caller)
@label=VerbMove
c$8D9D CALL $95ED          ; dark?
 $8DA0 JR NC,$8DAB         ; no: keep the direction
@isub=LD A,DIR_DOWN-1
 $8DA2 LD A,$09            ; in the dark: a random direction...
 $8DA4 CALL $9C9F          ; ... 0-9...
 $8DA7 INC A               ; ... plus 1: 1-10
 $8DA8 LD ($B6E7),A        ; CommandId := the random direction
